  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Behind the front, temperatures and humidity \nwill finally get knocked down closer to normal for early \nSeptember, with more comfortable conditions lasting into early \nnext week. Still some residual moisture lingering today and will\nlikely see sct showers into the early evening. Capped thunder\nchances at slight (20%) for the bulk of the area. Best chances \nof seeing more than a light rain shower are across the SWern\ncorner of Duplin co with an ongoing MCS approaching the area,\nbut think the worst of it will stay JUST S of the FA. Then \nEarly week trend is drier as high pressure builds in from the \nnorth. Highs in the mid 80s with lows in the 60s is fcst and is \nwhere our temps should be for the first half of September. Heat\nbuilds back from WED onward with strengthening Serly flow in the\nlow levels and ridging aloft expanding over ECONUS ahead of the\nnext upper trough to shunt a cold front toward ENC FRI and into\nthe weekend.",
